# Project Context
This project is an AI-Powered Video Interview Analysis System.

Tech Stack:
- Vision: MediaPipe (Face Landmarks), OpenCV
- Audio: Librosa (raw feature extraction), Whisper (STT), Turkish fine-tuned emotion models
- NLP: LLM-based semantic and emotion analysis


# Architecture Rules

- Each domain must be isolated in its own module:
  - vision/
  - audio/
  - nlp/
- No cross-module hidden dependencies.
- Never rewrite entire modules unless explicitly requested.
- When adding a new feature:
  1. First define the interface / class structure.
  2. Then implement the logic.


# Clean Code Rules

- Follow DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself).
- Apply Single Responsibility Principle.
- Keep functions explicit and readable.
- Avoid unnecessary abstraction layers.
- Avoid creating helper functions unless reused.
- Prefer flat and simple structure over deep class hierarchies.
- Never over-engineer.
- Prefer clarity over cleverness.


# Data Handling Rules

- Raw features must be normalized before downstream processing.
- Always use type hints.
- Do not introduce silent type coercion.


# Refactoring Rules

- When refactoring:
  - Do NOT change functionality.
  - Reduce unnecessary methods.
  - Inline single-use trivial helpers.
  - Keep files under reasonable size (~250-300 lines if possible).

# Pipeline Rules

- The pipeline must orchestrate modules only.
- No heavy logic inside pipeline.
- No feature extraction logic inside pipeline.
- Keep pipeline linear and readable.